# ─── Append these lines to your project's existing .gitignore ───
# Prevents session artifacts, signing keys, and local config from leaking into the repo.

# Session and planning artifacts (never commit these)
# Ignore all hidden files and folders (dotfiles/dotdirs) not explicitly tracked
.*
# ... but a blanket .* also swallows the repo plumbing, including .gitignore ITSELF, which means the
# ignore rules never reach a fresh clone, and .github, which means CI workflows can never be
# committed. Re-include the files that are genuinely part of the project. Found 2026-07-22.
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.editorconfig
!.github/
# Local tooling docs and working notes (suffix convention)
*.dev
openspec/
plan.md
scratch.md
notes.md
*.session
*.tmp

# Internal guiding / constitution docs - OPERATOR LAYER ONLY, never committed (even to private repos).
# They carry the ethos, agent rules, and project constitution; the live standard (esp/Orrery) ignores all
# four. The ONLY committed project docs are README.md / CHANGES.md / CONTRIBUTING.md / AUTHORS / LICENSE.
# Back-ported from Orrery's 2026-07-22 .gitignore fix after it shipped committed into oortery
# (INCIDENT 2026-11-15, .dev/INCIDENT-2026-11-15-guiding-docs-leak.md). orrery-locks.toml stays COMMITTED
# (public-safe CI lock manifest; see the results.json line below).
AGENTS.md
DIRECTION.md
PROJECT.md
TASKS.md
.env
.env*
*.env

# Keystores and signing keys (NEVER commit)
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
key.properties
keystore.properties
android/key.properties

# Local override files
local.properties
android/local.properties
*.local

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Build outputs
build/
dist/

# Python artifacts (Python/GTK4 and other Python projects)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Behavior-lock observed values (generated by lock probe in CI; the manifest IS committed)
orrery-locks.results.json

# dev test deps
node_modules/
